Configuring the GRUB Bootloader Configuration (grub.cfg)

1. Identify your target root partition name:

`lsblk`

2. Create /boot/grub/grub.cfg using your designated root partition:

cat << 'EOF' > /boot/grub/grub.cfg
set default=0
set timeout=5

insmod ext2
insmod part_gpt
insmod part_msdos

menuentry "Kinda Linux From Scratch (KLFS)" {
    search --no-floppy --set=root /
    echo "Loading Linux kernel..."
    linux /boot/vmlinuz root=/dev/sda1 rw quiet init=/sbin/init
    echo "Loading initial ramdisk..."
    initrd /boot/initramfs
}
EOF

3. Ensure correct file permissions on the configuration file:

`chmod 600 /boot/grub/grub.cfg`
